00:55:21,290 --> 00:55:27,290
Man of Steel is a 2013 superhero film based on the DC character Superman.

13
00:59:58,064 --> 01:00:04,064
Directed by Zack Snyder and written by David S.

14
01:04:34,838 --> 01:04:40,838
Goyer, who developed the story with producer Christopher Nolan, it is the first film in the DC Extended
Universe (DCEU), and a reboot of the Superman film series, depicting the character's origin story.

15
01:09:11,612 --> 01:09:17,612
Henry Cavill stars as Superman, alongside Amy Adams, Michael Shannon, Kevin
Costner, Diane Lane, Laurence Fishburne, and Russell Crowe.

16
01:13:48,387 --> 01:13:54,387
In the film, Clark Kent learns that he is a superpowered alien from the planet Krypton and assumes the role of
mankind's protector as Superman, making the choice to face General Zod and stop him from destroying humanity.

17
01:18:25,161 --> 01:18:31,161
Development began in 2008 when Warner Bros.

18
01:23:01,935 --> 01:23:07,935
took pitches from comic book writers, screenwriters, and
directors, opting to reboot the franchise.

19
01:27:38,709 --> 01:27:44,709
In 2009, a court ruling resulted in Jerry Siegel's family recapturing
the rights to Superman's origins and Siegel's copyright.

20
01:32:15,483 --> 01:32:21,483
The decision stated that Warner Bros.

21
01:36:52,258 --> 01:36:58,258
did not owe the families additional royalties from previous films, but if they did not begin production on a Superman film
by 2011, then the Shuster and Siegel estates would be able to sue for lost revenue on an unproduced film.

22
01:41:29,032 --> 01:41:35,032
Nolan pitched Goyer's idea after a story discussion on The Dark Knight Rises,
and Snyder was hired as the film's director in October 2010.

23
01:46:05,806 --> 01:46:11,806
Principal photography began in August 2011 in West Chicago,
Illinois, before moving to Vancouver and Plano, Illinois.

24
01:50:42,580 --> 01:50:48,580
Man of Steel premiered in the Alice Tully Hall in New York City on
June 10, 2013, and was released by Warner Bros.

25
01:55:19,354 --> 01:55:25,354
Pictures in the United States on June 14.

26
01:59:56,129 --> 02:00:02,129
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and was a commercial success, grossing $670 million
worldwide on a budget of $225–258 million, becoming the ninth-highest-grossing film of 2013.

27
02:04:32,903 --> 02:04:38,903
A sequel, Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice, was released in 2016.

28
02:09:09,677 --> 02:09:15,677
A further reboot, Superman, the first film in the DC Universe (DCU), was
released in 2025, and stars David Corenswet as the title character.

29
02:13:46,451 --> 02:13:52,451
The film explores themes of saving the world,
flying, hope, superhero, based on comic.

30
02:18:23,225 --> 02:18:29,225
The tone is thought_provoking.
